WEBVTT

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:09.884
["Here We Go" by Extreme Music playing]

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:18.601
[woman 1] I've known Justin
for four years now,

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.353
and he's one of my best friends.

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:21.855
Justin is definitely a bachelor,

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:24.399
but I think that he would be
a great boyfriend.

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:26.026
I know he wants to settle down.

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:32.323
[woman 2] Justin wants somebody
to meet his fire,

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.826
but there's some sort of inner turmoil

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:38.204
that he's fighting with, like,
who he's supposed to be with

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:40.331
versus who he wants to be with.

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:43.001
♪ So here we go... ♪

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:46.713
[woman 3] I do believe there's a woman
out there for Justin.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:48.590
I just feel like he hasn't met his match.

00:00:48.673 --> 00:00:52.761
I want Justin to find love
and his place in this world.

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:55.764
♪ Everybody in the shadows
Coming out today ♪

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:58.933
♪ Everybody in the shadows coming out
Here we go... ♪

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.853
[man] Justin is one of the most
real people I know,

00:01:01.936 --> 00:01:03.938
but he goes for party girls.

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:06.816
He just needs to find
an amazingly sincere woman.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.152
Like, Justin is an amazingly sincere man.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.237
♪ Here we go ♪

00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:13.573
♪ Here we go ♪

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.201
♪ Here we go ♪

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:30.507
♪ Here we go ♪

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.674
[music stops]

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:34.177
[Barbara] Hello!

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.428
-Barbara.
-Justin?

00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:37.138
-How are you?
-Oh, good. How are you?

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:38.640
-Nice to meet you. [laughs]
-[laughs]

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:40.475
-So nice to meet you.
-You look so pretty.

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:41.726
Thank you so much.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.729
-Is this your first blind date?
-It is my first blind date. I have never--

00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:46.731
I was hoping
that you could walk me through this.

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:50.860
[laughs] Oh, gosh! Yeah.
I have no idea where we're going.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.780
If not, we can both say
that this is our first blind date,

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:56.574
and then it started on Bourbon Street.

00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:57.909
-Perfect!
-Like, really...

00:01:57.992 --> 00:02:00.495
I don't think that you can go
any higher than that,

00:02:00.578 --> 00:02:03.957
or any more extreme than that,
to be honest with you.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.421
Oh, this is cute.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.465
It's a good vibe. Thank you.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.592
So, how are you today?

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.137
-Blessed and highly favored.
-Yeah?

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.054
How are you?

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.764
[Justin] I am super excited.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:22.725
I mean, blind dates are, like,
one of those things that...

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.312
just, like, things can either go
super right or super wrong.

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:27.313
-No. Yeah.
-But yeah,

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:29.774
first impressions, I mean...
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:33.778 --> 00:02:34.946
I'm Justin.

00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:37.407
-Hugs? Okay. Hi.
-I go in for hugs.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.117
-Okay.
-My palms get too sweaty

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.244
on these first dates.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.956
-My armpits are sweating right now.
-Okay, cool. Noted.

00:02:45.039 --> 00:02:46.666
-It's dripping like...
-[chuckles]

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:49.586
Oh. So, where are you from?

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.671
-I'm born and raised here.
-Me too!

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.341
I'm probably a hundred percent sure
that we have, like, mutual friends.

00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:58.261
-I'm pretty sure we have mutual friends--
-You're Filipino though, right?

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.972
-No, I'm not. Do I look Filipino?
-No, I'm just kidding you.

00:03:01.055 --> 00:03:02.849
-Are you Filipino?
-I am Filipino. [laughs]

00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:04.934
Why are you shaking my hand? Like...

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.312
-No, 'cause you're doing this.
-You stuck your hand out.

00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:09.689
-I'm sorry. All right.
-I'm sorry. I'm bad at dates.

00:03:09.772 --> 00:03:12.650
I need a shot of tequila...
and I'll get a cocktail too.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.861
-Let's go!
-Is that too much for a first date?

00:03:14.944 --> 00:03:15.945
No, no, no, no, no.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:18.281
I don't know how to flirt.
That's kinda my way of flirting.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.657
"Hey, um, let's take a shot."

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.368
You from here?

00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:25.288
I'm not. I am from, like a nomad.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.289
-Go ahead.
-Um...

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:29.709
born in Ohio,
moved to San Antonio, Texas,

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:32.295
and moved to Houston,
went to school in Alabama.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.714
-I'm gonna write this down. [laughs]
-I know, right?

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.841
Are your parents in Chalmette?

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:37.759
Yeah.

00:03:37.842 --> 00:03:40.887
They did the whole Hurricane Katrina thing
and they stayed...

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.472
-Okay.
-...and they rebuilt,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.057
and they're in the same house.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:47.018
'Cause it happened to me
during my senior year in high school.

00:03:47.101 --> 00:03:49.145
-Oh, wow. Where did y'all go?
-So, like...

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.272
So, we went to Houston.

00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:55.777
So, I went from this school
that had, like, 500 students

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:00.198
-to a school which had, like, 5,000 kids.
-[laughs]

00:04:00.281 --> 00:04:02.742
That Houston school was pretty rough.

00:04:02.825 --> 00:04:05.745
First day, I was eating at a lunch table
like this,

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.664
and then all of a sudden, like,

00:04:08.289 --> 00:04:12.418
somebody hops over the table,
and this brawl between New Orleans

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:14.087
and Houston happened.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.755
I was like, you know what?

00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:17.298
-No.
-I'll take the hurricane!

00:04:17.382 --> 00:04:19.592
-Yeah.
-That's... That's... crazy!

00:04:19.676 --> 00:04:20.593
Yeah.

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:23.054
-What is it that you do down here?
-I'm a singer.

00:04:23.137 --> 00:04:24.055
[Justin] Ooh!

00:04:24.138 --> 00:04:27.058
I don't really have residency anywhere.

00:04:27.141 --> 00:04:30.353
I just really put on my own shows,
and I travel and do other shows.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.021
-That's amazing!
-Yeah.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.439
I always wanted to be a singer.

00:04:33.523 --> 00:04:34.983
You always wanted to sing?

00:04:35.066 --> 00:04:37.902
-Yeah. I could never sing though.
-[laughs]

00:04:38.027 --> 00:04:40.822
But karaoke, I'm, like, great.
Karaoke I'm okay.

00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:43.741
-We might have to try. [laughs]
-Maybe after this...

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:47.036
I'm the photo-lead for an eyewear company
in New Orleans.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.163
-Nice!
-So what do you do?

00:04:49.247 --> 00:04:52.125
The main thing that I do, my nine-to-five,
is I work in finance.

00:04:52.208 --> 00:04:54.585
It's just so funny
because I'll start by saying,

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:56.212
"Yeah, I'm an accountant."
And they're like,

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:59.507
"Oh, so you're great with math?"
And I'm like, "No!"

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:02.427
And the next thing is, like,
"But you're Asian."

00:05:03.011 --> 00:05:06.014
And I'll be, like,
"Also a disappointment."

00:05:06.097 --> 00:05:07.765
My mom would love it
if I was an accountant.

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:10.810
-Anyone would love that.
-My mom was super happy

00:05:10.893 --> 00:05:12.979
that I went into accounting.

00:05:13.062 --> 00:05:15.982
Now, it's, like, "Oh, Justin,
you could have been a doctor.

00:05:16.065 --> 00:05:17.275
Why didn't you do that?"

00:05:17.358 --> 00:05:20.361
I'm, like, "You told me to do this!

00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:22.363
-[laughs]
-This was your idea!"

00:05:23.072 --> 00:05:27.744
So, like, around New Orleans,
what are your favorite things to do?

00:05:28.411 --> 00:05:29.370
Other than drink?

00:05:29.454 --> 00:05:33.166
Yeah, I mean, 'cause I can go on and on
about where I drink, right?

00:05:33.249 --> 00:05:35.209
I'm really not here that often
on the weekends.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.963
-I've been, like, full of weddings.
-Too many weddings?

00:05:39.047 --> 00:05:40.590
-Yeah!
-You have too many friends.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.342
-I know!
-Weddings are probably

00:05:42.425 --> 00:05:44.510
-my favorite things to go to.
-I know.

00:05:45.261 --> 00:05:46.512
-Oh, amazing!
-[waiter] Here you go.

00:05:46.596 --> 00:05:47.764
[Assata] Yes.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.558
-Oh, my goodness.
-[Assata] Oh, let's get it.

00:05:50.641 --> 00:05:51.601
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.144
To first blind dates.

00:05:53.978 --> 00:05:55.938
So, what kind of music do you dance to?

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.482
Uh, hip-hop.

00:05:57.565 --> 00:05:58.733
-Hip-hop? Okay, cool.
-Yeah.

00:05:58.816 --> 00:06:02.028
So are you kinda, like,
the break dancing...

00:06:02.111 --> 00:06:05.531
Or are you just kinda, like,
the smooth beat vibe?

00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:08.659
I mean I feel like
I can get into the smooth vibe...

00:06:08.743 --> 00:06:12.330
-Or are you, like...
-...but I can also go into, like... ayyy.

00:06:12.413 --> 00:06:13.956
-Okay! [laughs]
-Yeah. [laughs]

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.834
-No, we gonna stop that right here.
-[laughs]

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:20.129
This is-- We have had one drink
and we're not starting that!

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:22.590
No more, or you'll be carrying me home.
Period.

00:06:22.673 --> 00:06:24.675
-Okay.
-[laughs]

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:29.222
Every time that I get semi drunk,
I'm, like...

00:06:29.305 --> 00:06:31.766
-Let's go get a tattoo.
-I'm like, "Let's go get a tattoo."

00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:34.852
Then my mom is like, "Justin,
I'm going to cut your skin off

00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:36.479
-if you do that."
-[laughs] Aw.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.773
-Let me ask you, how old are you?
-I'm 31.

00:06:38.856 --> 00:06:41.234
That sounds about right,
'cause Asians don't raisin.

00:06:41.317 --> 00:06:42.527
[both laughing]

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.112
-Guess my age.
-Twenty...

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:46.489
-Twenty?
-...eight?

00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:49.992
-Twenty eight?
-Thirty?

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:52.995
Oh, I know you did not just--
Thirty! Really?

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:53.913
Twenty...

00:06:53.996 --> 00:06:56.207
All right,
this date needs to end right now.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:57.750
-I'm sorry.
-[scoffs]

00:06:57.834 --> 00:07:00.002
-You can see your way out!
-[laughs]

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:01.504
-You can see your way out!
-No.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:04.340
If I had to guess,
I'd probably say, like, 25.

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:06.175
-Twenty six, actually.
-Oh!

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:08.845
You know you're lying.
You said 20 or 30 at first.

00:07:09.971 --> 00:07:11.722
[waiter] Pardon my interruption.
Our table is ready.

00:07:11.806 --> 00:07:13.516
-Oh, amazing.
-[bartender] You wanna follow me.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:14.725
-Sure.
-Cool.

00:07:14.809 --> 00:07:15.810
I'll get your chair.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.520
-Thank you.
-After you.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.571
[waiter] Here's a couple of menus.

00:07:26.654 --> 00:07:27.613
Thank you.

00:07:27.697 --> 00:07:29.282
[waiter]
Are we good with the drinks for now?

00:07:29.365 --> 00:07:31.117
Let's do another shot of tequila.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.535
-Yep. Yeah.
-All right, yeah.

00:07:33.369 --> 00:07:36.164
I kinda wanna switch to tequila
now that you've been drinking tequila.

00:07:36.247 --> 00:07:38.583
-[laughs]
-All right, so you're ready to party.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.085
[laughing]

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:42.920
I might get the chicken liver mousse.

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:45.298
-I've never had liver...
-Chicken liver mousse.

00:07:45.381 --> 00:07:47.091
...but I'm down to try it tonight.

00:07:47.341 --> 00:07:48.217
Let's do it.

00:07:48.509 --> 00:07:51.554
-See, that's how first dates go great.
-[giggles]

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.432
Did you grow up lower middle class?

00:07:55.433 --> 00:07:58.186
I feel like I grew up
mid to lower middle class.

00:07:58.269 --> 00:07:59.395
I don't know.

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.564
-So, growing up...
-[laughs] It's always really vague.

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:04.484
...it was more like a community-type thing
where we grew up,

00:08:04.567 --> 00:08:07.278
and we kinda, like,
stayed in our little circle.

00:08:07.361 --> 00:08:09.780
I could have been an upper-class person,

00:08:09.864 --> 00:08:12.825
but, like, according to people
outside of the city,

00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:14.118
I was probably broke.

00:08:14.619 --> 00:08:16.287
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:19.290
I went to a lot of private schools,
which I was very thankful for,

00:08:19.373 --> 00:08:22.460
but we were, like, Payless
and a hand-me-down.

00:08:22.543 --> 00:08:23.377
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:23.461 --> 00:08:27.590
And I was, like, why does everyone have
this Micheal Kors bag...

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:28.508
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:28.591 --> 00:08:30.426
...and this pink Razr phone?

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.679
-Why can't I have a pink Razr phone?
-Razr phone! [chuckles]

00:08:33.763 --> 00:08:35.348
So, as far as photography goes,

00:08:35.431 --> 00:08:37.683
are there certain things
that you wanna photograph?

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:40.603
I'm really into outside, natural lighting.

00:08:40.686 --> 00:08:43.397
-Yeah.
-Really flowy, motion blur...

00:08:43.481 --> 00:08:44.524
I'm, like, Photoshop queen.

00:08:44.607 --> 00:08:45.858
-I can do anything.
-Really?

00:08:45.942 --> 00:08:47.777
'Cause I've always wanted
to go to England.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.321
I'll just take a picture of you
out here in New Orleans,

00:08:50.404 --> 00:08:52.365
-and Photoshop you in London.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:52.448 --> 00:08:54.784
-Put me in front of Buckingham Palace.
-That's it.

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:57.662
-Next to the Queen. [laughs]
-Okay, next Instagram post! [laughs]

00:08:57.745 --> 00:08:59.247
[laughing]

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:03.084
Something I do to kill time,
I don't know if you are familiar with this

00:09:03.167 --> 00:09:05.253
but I like to do mukbangs.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:08.798
It's, like, you have a shitload of food
in front of you,

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:10.550
and you record yourself eating,

00:09:10.633 --> 00:09:12.969
but you're doing it live,
and people are watching you.

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:16.722
For example, I'll have a plate, like,
of 50 chicken wings,

00:09:16.806 --> 00:09:18.683
-and I'll just start eating chicken wings.
-[laughs]

00:09:18.766 --> 00:09:20.017
That's amazing.

00:09:20.142 --> 00:09:22.645
Have you ever done
that hot ramen challenge?

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:25.648
-The two times spicy?
-Yes, I did that on my stream before.

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:26.732
I did that on my stream.

00:09:26.816 --> 00:09:31.404
-How did you deal with that? [laughs]
-It was bad. My asshole was burning.

00:09:31.487 --> 00:09:35.866
Oh, no, baby! Oh, no. Oh, no. Oh, no.

00:09:41.622 --> 00:09:42.999
That looks beautiful.

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.500
[Assata] It does. It's very colorful.

00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:47.670
-All right, so I'm gonna let you try this.
-I'm gonna pray.

00:09:48.671 --> 00:09:50.923
-Oh. All right, are you ready?
-Oh, you pray?

00:09:51.007 --> 00:09:53.259
-No.
-You trying to pray together?

00:09:53.342 --> 00:09:56.679
Ain't nothing gonna make my mama happier
than if we do this.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:58.014
So, go ahead. Yeah.

00:09:58.097 --> 00:10:01.267
Heavenly Father, thank you so much
for this food that we have received.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.853
Thank you for the nourishment.
Thank you for this opportunity.

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:07.356
And bless this food.
In Jesus's name, amen.

00:10:07.481 --> 00:10:08.482
[both exhale]

00:10:08.566 --> 00:10:11.193
-I feel it, and appreciate that.
-You feel it.

00:10:11.694 --> 00:10:14.071
-Well, bon appétit. Let's try this food.
-Yeah, for sure.

00:10:16.198 --> 00:10:18.117
-Ooh!
-Go ahead.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.660
[chews loudly] Beau, beau.

00:10:19.744 --> 00:10:21.037
[laughs]

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.205
It's good. It's flavorful, just like me.

00:10:25.041 --> 00:10:26.834
-Yeah. [chuckles]
-Okay.

00:10:27.835 --> 00:10:31.756
-Let me take a sip of my water.
-It's deep and flavorful, just like me.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:34.884
-I can agree with that.
-Thank you. [chuckles]

00:10:35.426 --> 00:10:40.056
No, like, I appreciate when a woman
can describe herself,

00:10:40.139 --> 00:10:44.060
or describe what she's feeling,
and how she deals with things.

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:45.436
-I appreciate that.
-Aw. Aw!

00:10:45.519 --> 00:10:47.730
-Thank you, I appreciate you too.
-Don't cry. Don't cry.

00:10:48.189 --> 00:10:51.067
You, pretty much being from here,

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:55.321
-how is your dating life in New Orleans?
-Dating life.

00:10:55.404 --> 00:10:58.074
Oh, man, I have tried, I've really tried.

00:10:58.157 --> 00:11:01.035
[chuckles] I've given it a valiant effort.

00:11:01.118 --> 00:11:02.119
[laughs]

00:11:02.203 --> 00:11:05.206
Where are these guys
that I align with in New Orleans?

00:11:05.289 --> 00:11:08.125
Where are they?
I'm really struggling to find them.

00:11:08.209 --> 00:11:09.960
